# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in real values before deploying.

# Used to sign session cookies. Generate a long random string for production,
# e.g. `openssl rand -base64 32`. The app falls back to an insecure dev value
# if this is unset, which is fine for local development only.
SESSION_SECRET=

# Optional: override the local SQLite database file location.
# DATABASE_PATH=./data/hairtopia.db

# --- MTN MoMo Collections (Ghana) — OPTIONAL, prepared but not required ---
# Mobile money at checkout falls back to a clear "not configured" error until
# ALL THREE of these are set with real MTN MoMo API credentials for a live
# Collections subscription. Cash/card/bank-transfer payments work without
# these. See src/lib/payments/provider.ts for exactly how they're used.
# MTN_MOMO_API_USER=
# MTN_MOMO_API_KEY=
# MTN_MOMO_SUBSCRIPTION_KEY=
# MTN_MOMO_BASE_URL=https://sandbox.momodeveloper.mtn.com
# MTN_MOMO_ENVIRONMENT=sandbox
# MTN_MOMO_CALLBACK_SECRET=
# ^ Shared secret the webhook route checks against an incoming
#   X-Callback-Secret header. MTN doesn't HMAC-sign callbacks, so this is
#   the actual recommended verification mechanism for this integration —
#   generate a long random value and register it however your MTN
#   integration lets you attach custom auth to the callback URL.
#   Leaving it unset means the webhook accepts any request shaped like a
#   valid callback — fine for local testing, NOT for production.

# --- Web Push (PWA lock-screen/background notifications) — OPTIONAL ---
# Without these, push is gracefully skipped (in-app notifications still
# work); "Enable notifications" in the app will show "not configured".
# Generate a real pair with: npx web-push generate-vapid-keys
# VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
# VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:admin@hairtopiastudio.com

# --- Scheduled jobs (appointment & deposit reminders) — OPTIONAL ---
# Required for /api/cron/reminders to do anything. Without it, the endpoint
# returns 503 and sends nothing — it is never silently open. Generate a
# long random value and configure your scheduler (cron, Vercel Cron, a
# GitHub Action, etc.) to call the endpoint with:
#   Authorization: Bearer <this value>
# CRON_SECRET=
